    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #297\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-270-review-debt-05-12-validate-the-inbox-c-thr_pvjvy9vcey`.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #270. Addresses the two unresolved post-merge review findings from #101:\n\n1. **Unvalidated capture date** (`backend/packages/data/src/inbox/inboxStore.ts`): `createInboxItemWithClient` now validates `date` with `DateTime.fromISO(input.date).isValid` after the existing falsy checks, throwing `ValidationError(\"Inbox items require a valid ISO date for 'date'\", { field: \"date\" })` for a truthy-but-unparseable string, before any write is attempted. `date`/`time` are still stored verbatim on success — no server-side substitution. `time` is intentionally left unvalidated, per the issue's scope.\n\n2. **Silently truncated type list** (`backend/packages/data/src/inbox/inboxTypesStore.ts`): `listActiveInboxTypes` now pages through `listItems` using its cursor, accumulating results until `nextCursor` is `null`, instead of hard-coding `limit: 200`. The returned `InboxTypeSummary[]` shape (`id`, `emoji`, `label`) is unchanged, so no caller needs to change.\n\nAdded tests in `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/inboxPipeline.test.ts`:\n- an Inbox item with `date: \"not-a-date\"` is rejected with `ValidationError` on field `date`, and no Inbox or Journal item is written;\n- `listActiveInboxTypes` returns all 210 active types created in a single transaction (each with `status: \"active\"` explicitly set, since `listActiveInboxTypes` filters on that field).\n\n## Test plan\n- `pnpm -r run build` — all 7 backend packages build cleanly.\n- Full backend test suite (`vitest run`) — 24 test files, 315 tests, all passing.\n- `tsc --noEmit` on the `data` package — clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
